  "definition": "Precise Point Positioning, or PPP, estimates position from precise satellite orbit and clock products together with undifferenced pseudorange and carrier-phase observations at a single user receiver. It does not need a surveyed reference station close to that user, although global reference networks and processing centres are still required to generate the precise products.[^1]",
